--------------------- CableDyn Input File ------------------------------------
Laid power cable in a 1.2 m/s cross current held by anisotropic seabed friction
-- A 230 m, 0.20 m, 80 kg/m cable hangs from a held hang-off 14 m below the surface (End A) and
-- lies on a flat 80 m seabed for about half its length to a seabed anchor 200 m away in +X (End B).
-- A 1.2 m/s uniform current in +Y crosses the laid run. Seabed friction is anisotropic in the
-- OrcaFlex axial/normal sense: 0.3 along the local cable axis, 1.0 across it. The current loads the
-- laid run across its axis, so the lateral coefficient decides how far it slides before friction
-- holds it; the static solve finds the slid equilibrium and the 10 s dynamic run keeps it at rest.
-- Change the two frictionMu* rows (for example to one 0.3 frictionMu row) to compare.
-- The cable is tension-only (EI = 0), as for a laid-cable route survey.
